FigJam is mainly a collaborative whiteboarding and brainstorming tool, not a full UI design tool.

It is primarily used for:
=========================
Mind maps
Brainstorming
Sticky notes
User flows
Wireframe planning
Team collaboration
UX workshops
Diagrams
Planning sessions

FigJam vs Figma
================
Feature	              FigJam	          Figma
=======               ======            ======
Mind Mapping	        Excellent	        Basic
Brainstorming	        Excellent	        Limited
Sticky Notes	        Yes	              No
Whiteboard	          Yes	              No
UI Design	            Basic	            Professional
Prototyping	          Minimal	          Advanced
Components	          Limited	          Full support
Developer Handoff	    Limited	          Full
UX Workshops	        Excellent	        Moderate

Simple Explanation
==================
FigJam
======
Think of it as:
===============
a digital whiteboard
brainstorming canvas
collaborative planning board

Used BEFORE actual UI design.

Figma
=====
Think of it as:

professional UI/UX design software
interface creation tool
prototyping tool

Used FOR actual UI design and development handoff.

Typical Workflow
================
Ideas → FigJam → Figma → Prototype → Development

Example:
========
Brainstorm app features in FigJam
=================================
Create mind maps and user flows
Plan screens and navigation
Move to Figma
Design actual UI screens

